{"kind":"promise","text":"Builder accepts E1 first stage: a read-only inventory and settlement-planning ledger of Artroom-owned external resources. Before any call, as the request asks, here is what I will use. Identity and custody: Cloudflare account 6e953d231f1c9aadffbf59537a82e13a with the operator's existing wrangler login; the login token is read from the local wrangler configuration inside the process, sent only to api.cloudflare.com, and never printed, logged or written; 'wrangler whoami' may be run once to refresh an expired login. GitHub repository generalbusiness-ai/artroom with the operator's existing gh login. Routes, GET only: Workers scripts list, and for each script whose name starts with artroom its deployments, versions (first page), settings and bindings (secret bindings appear by name only) and schedules; Durable Object namespaces list; container applications list and registry image list; Artifacts namespaces gitseq-spike, gitseq-spike-import and artroom-public: repository listing with cursor, and token metadata per Artroom-owned repository (IDs, scope, expiry; no token text is returned by a listing). GitHub, GET only: repository settings, workflows, the last 30 workflow runs, deploy keys, and the names only of Actions secrets and variables. Local: existence, owner and mode of credential files and release directories with ls; no file content is read. Limits: 100 items per page, at most 20 pages per listing, each listing marked complete or incomplete with its last cursor. I will not run deploy, cleanup or measurement scripts, create or revoke any token, delete or change anything, or install anything. Where a read cannot enumerate a duty, the ledger records the gap and its owner. Delivery: one document-only commit on request/e1-inventory, with the ledger and the redacted observation data, head reported here.","body":{"branch":"request/e1-inventory"}}